<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starship-flight-15 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Starship Flight 15 / Starlink 31-2 (Starbase OLP-2) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT ILLUSTRATIVE. SpaceX Starship Flight 15 (Starlink 31-2, 26 V3 satellites) from Starbase OLP-2. First attempt to catch both stages (catch / deorbit not in this file).
T0 2026-11-13T22:45:00Z (Fri Nov 13 2:45 p.m. PST / 4:45 p.m. CT), 75-minute window, pending regulatory approval, per SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/starship-flight-15. LL2 status To Be Confirmed, window 22:45Z–00:00Z (id 0f867f0c-5422-4d44-93b8-d7faaae7019b).
Event times: SpaceX Flight 15 published timeline https://www.spacex.com/launches/starship-flight-15: Max-Q T+00:00:58, Super Heavy MECO T+00:02:19 (139 s), hot-stage / ship ignition / separation T+00:02:21 (141 s), Starship engine cutoff T+00:08:09 (489 s). File ends at ascent cutoff. Orbital insertion burn T+00:26:10–26:30 and payload deploy complete T+01:17:40 are in the sim file only.
Azimuth 107.53 deg: great-circle bearing from the LL2 pad (25.99677N, 97.15799W) to the far-edge midpoint (20.6042N, 81.6500W) of NAVAREA IV 1080/26 Area A (Gulf / Yucatan launch corridor). Non-rotating i ~31.01 deg. Hazard-area azimuth kept (NOTAM-first). https://space-notices.com/notice/nav-warning-NAVAREA%20IV%201080%2F26
Orbit: SpaceX publishes ~275 km after the T+26:10 insertion burn, on a passively safe suborbital profile then an orbit-raising burn (F15 official text; F14 official analog). This surrogate ends at ascent cutoff; altitude knots are the retuned 3DOF sim (fitted to an ASSUMED −40 × 275 km pre-insertion ellipse, 1081 s before apogee). Vehicle figures from https://www.spacex.com/vehicles/starship/technical-specifications and the 12 May 2026 V3 update.
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published SpaceX F15 timeline, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times): 0:0, 58:9.8, 139:86.8, 141:90.2, 489:162.6
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.408 km/s (circular v at 162.6 km geodetic ascent-cutoff altitude minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+489 s. File ends at Starship engine cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 25.996770N -97.157990E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=107.53 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-13T22:45:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
